<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Washukanni</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Washukanni was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a>, probably located in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khabur-river">Khabur</a> valley of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, though its exact site has not been confirmed. The Mitanni Empire profile records that it was sacked by the Hittite king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suppiluliuma-i">Suppiluliuma I</a> around 1340 BCE. This was a decisive blow to Mitanni's independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/washukanni.jpg" alt="Washukanni" width="320" height="227" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Goran tek-en · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N-Mesopotamia_and_Syria_english.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
